      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Using `LOG_MODULE_REGISTER` in a header file will cause One Definition Rule (ODR) violations and linker errors if this header is included in multiple `.cc` files (as it currently is in `fpsensor_frame_size.cc` and `fpsensor_get_frame.cc`).\n\nIn Zephyr, `LOG_MODULE_REGISTER` must be called exactly once per module, typically in a `.c` or `.cc` file. \n\n**Suggestions:**\n1. Move `LOG_MODULE_REGISTER(fpsensor_test_utils, ...)` into a new `fpsensor_test_utils.cc` file, and use `LOG_MODULE_DECLARE(fpsensor_test_utils, ...)` here in the header.\n2. Alternatively, for a simple test helper like this, you can just use `printk` or `ztest_print` instead of the Zephyr logging subsystem to avoid needing a separate `.cc` file entirely.",
